  "amendment": "Amended before any candidate was scored and before any ensemble was built (the seven original learner chains were already running on arcw1/arcw2/arcw4 with the runner at the hash recorded under parents.learner_code_run_adsb_learner): two learner variants with the ADS-B-residual target were added (target = label minus the observed ADS-B taxi, takeoff minus motion start, on matched rows; the plain label elsewhere; the offset is added back), fitted on arcw3 with the runner at the hash recorded under parents.learner_code_run_adsb_learner_amended; ensembles ens_v15_res and ens_v15_mix and their six blend candidates were added; nothing else changed. Rationale: a tree ensemble reproduces the near-identity relation between the label and the observed taxi only piecewise; fitting the gap removes that burden (the same device as the v12 residual on v9 and the NM-residual learner).",
