  "prediction_postprocess": "adsb-surface-residual-v15-v1",
  "prior_evidence": "Declared after v14 (official 243.5805, 1st of 148 at 00:51 UTC 16 September). Diagnostics run before this declaration on the recorded v14 development predictions: (1) LIRF: even gate-covered LIRF segments show the airport block time a median 373-495 s before the ADS-B motion start with an interquartile spread of about 400 s (EDDF gate rows: within 60 s), so the LIRF label is not the observable pushback; a LIRF-only residual (matched non-population rows, v12 features, leave-one-month-out Jul<->Nov, Jan has no LIRF coverage) was WORSE than v14 on both months (+0.17% / +2.01% at weight 1.0; +0.04% / +0.47% at 0.5); LIRF stays excluded from every candidate, as in v11-v14. (2) First-point geometry features (first-point and stand latitude/longitude, bearing, 250 m grid cell) added to the v12 residual: null (+0.05% / -0.04% / -0.14% on Jan / Jul / Nov versus v12); not declared. (3) Blend structure on the recorded predictions: per-airport or per-match-status weights and a three-way least-squares stack (v12, LightGBM, CatBoost) fitted leave-one-month-out are null or worse than the fixed w = 0.6 mean (best mean +0.02%); not declared. (4) The remaining non-LIRF error is spread over ordinary matched and unmatched rows (Nov 2025: matched 27.5% of SSE, unmatched 34.8%, LIRF 37.7%); the lever declared here is learner strength and diversity: seed bagging, a longer CatBoost (its 6,000-round cap bound on both v14 folds), a deeper column-subsampled LightGBM and a one-day-label-cleaned LightGBM. No learner variant listed here had been fitted before this declaration.",
